Z||000000||fiero56||06-18-2000||11:58 PM||||I started the Fiero this morning to move it into the garage to begin installing power acessories on it. I parked it in the garage, shut off the engine, but I left it in neutral(not thinking clearly), and set the parking brake(I fiddled forever with it, but got it to work until I am able get a new cable in). Well, the damn drivers side cable gave way while I was in the house getting the window motors. I come out a minute or two later, and my Formula is out in the street. It rolled down the drive, accross the street, over two bushes and a flower bed(all owned by my neigbor accross the street). I actaully took the responsibility of telling hom when he got home. Well, instead of finishing my project, my only day off work tommorrwo will be spent doing "lots of yard work" for him. Damnit! If I only would have ordered that cable LAST week instead of planning to order it THIS week.<P><BR>No damage to the Fiero at all. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||8
